    <statement><p>Find an antiderivative <m>G</m> of 
<m>\displaystyle g(z)= \frac{1}{z^{6}}</m></p>
<p><m>G(z) =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{-1}{5z^{5}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>g(z) = z^{-6}</m>.  Then <m>g(z) = G'(z)</m>, so <m>G(z)</m> must
have the form <m>G(z) = -\frac{1}{5} z^{-5}</m> (or this, plus any
constant). 



</solution>
